# M5 — posture rule 3 (OWNERSHIP) made unmatchable.
#
# V4: table OWNERSHIP bypasses RLS under ENABLE independently of rolsuper and
# rolbypassrls. Rule 3 is the only thing in the schema that notices statesman_app owning
# a public table. When the adversarial pass ran, posture.test.ts carried controls for
# rules 4, 1, 2, 5, 6 and 8 and none for rule 3, so the rule could be made to match
# nothing and the suite stayed green at 44/44.
#
# A/B partner: MS1 breaks rule 4 in the same function and the same way. Both are CAUGHT
# now; if one ever regresses to ESCAPED while the other does not, the difference is the
# control and not the harness.
id: M5
title: posture rule 3 OWNERSHIP compares relowner to a role name that cannot exist
expect: caught
proves: posture rule 3 (canon 4.8 rule 3, V4) has a control that names the offending table
expect-test: [M5] raises ST099 for a public table owned by authenticated

file: supabase/migrations/20261021140500_verify_security_posture.sql
count: 1
@@FIND
      and pg_get_userbyid(c.relowner) in ('anon','authenticated','service_role')
@@REPLACE
      and pg_get_userbyid(c.relowner) in ('__never_a_role__')
@@END
